    "title": "UFL schedule: How to watch and stream the Week 1 games",
    "text": "March 28, 2026, 8:30 a.m. MTWelcome back, spring football.The 2026 United Football League schedule kicked off on Friday night with the Louisville Kings hosting the Birmingham Stallions in Kentucky. Three more games are on deck this weekend.The action continues on Saturday with the St. Louis Battlehawks hosting the DC Defenders in Missouri at 10:00 a.m. MT (noon ET) on Saturday, March 28. That game will be televised on ESPN and available to stream on FuboTV.Up next, the Dallas Renegades will host the Houston Gamblers in Texas at 2:00 p.m. MT (4:00 p.m. ET) on Saturday, March 28. The rivalry matchup will be televised on Fox and available to stream on FuboTV.To wrap up the weekend slate, the Orlando Storm will host the Columbus Aviators in Florida at 6:00 p.m. MT (8:00 p.m. ET) on Sunday, March 29. That game will be televised on ESPN and available to stream on FuboTV.UFL Week 1 ScheduleMarch 28: St. Louis vs. DC at 10:00 a.m. MT (ESPN)March 28: Dallas vs. Houston at 2:00 p.m. MT (Fox)March 29: Orlando vs. Columbus at 6:00 p.m. MT (ESPN)There are 12 former Broncos players suiting up in the UFL this spring, plus a player-turned-coach. Denver has found talent from spring football leagues in each of the last four offseasons, adding long snapper Mitchell Fraboni (2022, USFL), quarterback Ben DiNucci (2023, XFL), outside linebacker Dondrea Tillman (2024, UFL) and cornerback Mario Goodrich (2025, UFL). We'll see if that trend continues after the 2026 season wraps up in June.Social: Follow Broncos Wire on Facebook and Twitter/X! Did you know: These 25 celebrities are Broncos fans.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
